    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n44 Oak Road is a charming three-bedroom terraced residence tucked away in a quiet cul-de-sac setting conveniently located just off the Malahide Road. Built in the 1930s and extending to approximately 75 sq.m (807 sq.ft), the property offers well-proportioned rooms and a practical layout throughout. The accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway leading to a spacious living room to the front of the property, complete with a feature fireplace and access to understairs storage. To the rear is a second reception room, providing excellent versatility for modern family living. Off this room is a recently upgraded shower room and a separate kitchen. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms. The generous principal bedroom is positioned to the front of the house and benefits from good built-in storage, with potential to incorporate an en-suite bathroom. To the rear are two further bedrooms, both offering comfortable accommodation and flexibility for family living, guest use or a home office. The property presents an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking a home with character and convenience, while offering plenty of scope to modernise, personalise and create a home tailored to their own tastes and requirements.\n\nGardens\n\nOutside, the property benefits from off-street parking to the front on a concrete driveway, bordered by colourful flower beds. To the rear, there is a low-maintenance garden, primarily laid in gravel, providing an ideal space for outdoor relaxation with minimal upkeep. A block-built garden shed with electricity offers excellent secure storage or potential for use as a workshop/hobby space, it is conveniently plumbed for a washing machine and dryer. Further outdoor features include an external tap, additional storage sheds and the added convenience of pedestrian rear lane access, a highly desirable feature for a terraced home.\n\nLocation\n\nOak Road is positioned in a highly desirable residential location, this popular neighbourhood is close to an abundance of local amenities, including a selections of shops on Collins Avenue, Artane Shopping Centre, St Anne's Park and a short distance from Clontarf Village with an abundances of cafés, restaurants and bars. The location also benefits from exceptional connectivity, with easy access to the M50 motorway, Beaumont Hospital, Dublin Airport, Eastpoint Business Park and Dublin City Centre. Additionally, a variety of bus routes on the Malahide Road provide convenient transport options to the city centre and beyond. \n\nIf you would like a viewing, please email us or call the office directly on 01 8336555 to arrange an appointment with the agent Geraldine Hennessy. If you wish to place an offer, please visit www.sherryfitz.ie where you can register to make an offer on this property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGround Floor - \n\n\nSitting Room - 3.7m x 4.65m\n\n\nLiving Room - 4.7m x 2.35m\n\n\nKitchen - 3m x 2.2m\n\n\nShower Room - 1.6m x 2.2m\n\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.8m x 3.2m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 2m x 3.7m\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.2m x 2.6m\n\n\n"
      },
